        injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 2.0 (A fully electronic, highly advanced sequential fuel injection system managed by the Bosch ME 2.0 architecture. Utilizes a Hot-Film Mass Air Flow sensor and completely avoids the biodegradable wiring issues of early 90s models. Very reliable, but sensitive to vacuum leaks from aging PCV hoses.)",
        engineLifespan: "400 000 - 500 000+ km (The M113 V8 is widely considered one of the most reliable V8 engines Mercedes-Benz ever manufactured. The aluminum block with Silitec cylinder liners is incredibly wear-resistant. The engine will effortlessly outlast the W202 chassis; the true enemies are structural rust and harmonic balancer failure.)",
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M113 uses a 3-valve-per-cylinder design with a twin-spark ignition system to maximize low-end torque and improve emissions. Power delivery is exceptionally smooth, linear, and brutally powerful.)",
        ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.0 (A rock-solid engine management system integrated perfectly with the 5G-Tronic automatic transmission. The ECU is highly robust, but it relies on a Crankshaft Position Sensor that is notorious for failing when hot, leaving the car stranded until it cools down.)",
