        yearRange: "2000-2002",
        timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M111 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain that represents the absolute zenith of Mercedes-Benz engineering before the cost-cutting era. Unlike modern, lightweight single-row chains that stretch and snap, this heavy-duty timing system is a genuine 'lifetime' component. The massive steel chain glides on highly reinforced polymer guide rails and is kept under optimal, constant tension by a hydraulic tensioner that relies entirely on clean, high-pressure engine oil. If the owner strictly adheres to 10 000 kilometer oil change intervals using high-quality synthetic lubricants, this timing chain assembly will rarely require servicing before 400 000 to 500 000 kilometers.)",
        injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 2.1 (This engine features a fully electronic, highly advanced sequential fuel injection system managed by the Bosch ME architecture. It utilizes a highly accurate Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor to measure incoming air, combined with an electronic throttle body that seamlessly integrates with the vehicle's traction control and cruise control systems. The system utilizes modern Bosch EV6 solenoid injectors that provide excellent fuel atomization. The injection system itself is incredibly reliable and virtually never suffers from wiring shorts, completely avoiding the biodegradable wiring nightmares of the early 1990s.)",
        engineLifespan: "400 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the M111 is a massive, heavily reinforced cast-iron engine block that is globally legendary for its near-indestructible durability. Because this specific C 200 K variant utilizes a robust internal rotating assembly operating at a relatively conservative 163 horsepower, the physical engine components—including the forged steel crankshaft and heavy-duty connecting rods—are almost completely unstressed. Wear on the cylinder walls and bearings is virtually nonexistent even after decades of heavy use. The engine will effortlessly outlast the early W203 chassis that surrounds it, provided rust is kept at bay. The supercharger bearings are the only true wear point.)",
        turboType: "Supercharged (Equipped with an Eaton M45 Roots-type positive displacement supercharger. Unlike the later M271 engines, this specific pre-facelift M111 supercharger DOES utilize an electromagnetic clutch on earlier iterations or a bypass valve system to engage boost. It provides incredibly strong, instantaneous low-end torque right off idle, entirely eliminating the lag associated with turbochargers. The power delivery is exceptionally linear, refined, and deeply muscular for a 4-cylinder engine. The specialized aviation oil inside the supercharger snout must be replaced every 100 000 kilometers to prevent the internal planetary gears from running dry and self-destructing.)",
        ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.1 (A highly sophisticated and incredibly reliable electronic engine control module that serves as the absolute mastermind of the powertrain. It flawlessly coordinates fuel pressure monitoring, supercharger bypass actuation, electronic throttle actuation, and complex immobilizer security protocols. The ECU is fully OBD-II compliant, making modern diagnostics, live data logging, and troubleshooting incredibly straightforward for modern mechanics. Because this engine is heavily over-engineered, the Bosch ECU rarely fails unless subjected to severe water intrusion from blocked cowl drains.)",
        euroStandard: "Euro 3",
        maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The heavy cast-iron block, robust cooling jackets, and forged internal rotating assembly of the M111 are vastly overbuilt for the factory 163 horsepower output. The absolute limiting factor for producing massive horsepower is the flow capacity of the Eaton M45 supercharger, which superheats the intake air if spun too fast. The bottom end can easily, reliably handle significant boost pressure all day long. Enthusiasts seeking extreme performance frequently install smaller supercharger pulleys or bolt on custom turbocharger setups, unlocking immense power without ever stressing the factory connecting rods or pistons.)",
