    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M112 AMG utilizes a highly reinforced duplex (double-row) timing chain that represents the absolute zenith of Mercedes-Benz engineering before the cost-cutting era. Unlike the disastrous single-row chains found in 4-cylinder models, this heavy-duty timing system is a genuine 'lifetime' component. The massive steel chain glides on highly reinforced polymer guide rails and is kept under optimal tension by a hydraulic tensioner. If the owner adheres to strict 10 000 kilometer oil change intervals using high-quality synthetic lubricants, this timing chain assembly will rarely require servicing before 400 000 kilometers.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 2.8 (This engine features a fully electronic, highly advanced sequential fuel injection system managed by the robust Bosch ME architecture. It utilizes a highly accurate Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor to measure the massive volume of pressurized air forced in by the twin-screw supercharger. The system utilizes modern, high-capacity Bosch EV6 solenoid injectors that provide excellent fuel atomization. The injection system itself is incredibly reliable and virtually never suffers from the capillary oil wicking issues that destroy the computers on later 4-cylinder M271 models.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 400 000+ km (The mechanical core of the M112 is a massive, heavily reinforced aluminum engine block with Silitec liners that is globally legendary for its near-indestructible durability. The internal rotating assembly was heavily upgraded by AMG with forged connecting rods and a specialized crankshaft to handle the immense 450 Nm of torque. Wear on the cylinder walls and bearings is virtually nonexistent even after decades of heavy use. The engine block will effortlessly outlast the W203 chassis, but its ultimate demise is frequently caused by catastrophic cooling failures, specifically the Valeo radiator destroying the transmission or the intercooler leaking into the cylinders.)",
    turboType: "Supercharged (Equipped with a highly efficient IHI twin-screw positive displacement supercharger paired with a water-to-air intercooler. The supercharger utilizes an electromagnetic clutch to engage only when requested by the ECU, improving fuel economy while cruising. When engaged, it provides incredibly violent, instantaneous low-end torque right off idle, entirely eliminating the lag associated with turbochargers. However, the water-to-air intercooler core located directly under the supercharger frequently leaks coolant into the engine, and the Bosch intercooler fluid circulation pump fails constantly, disabling the supercharger entirely due to high intake air temperatures.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.8 (A highly sophisticated and incredibly reliable electronic engine control module flashed with bespoke AMG mapping. It flawlessly coordinates high-pressure fuel delivery, supercharger clutch engagement, electronic throttle actuation, and complex immobilizer security protocols. The ECU is fully OBD-II compliant, making modern diagnostics, live data logging, and troubleshooting incredibly straightforward for mechanics. Because this engine is heavily over-engineered, the Bosch ECU rarely fails unless subjected to severe water intrusion from blocked cowl drains near the windshield.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "450+ hp (The aluminum block, robust cooling jackets, and forged internal rotating assembly of the 3.2L AMG V6 are vastly overbuilt for the factory 354 horsepower output. The absolute limiting factor for producing massive horsepower is the flow capacity of the IHI supercharger, which superheats the intake air if spun too fast, and the efficiency of the stock heat exchanger. Enthusiasts seeking extreme performance frequently install smaller supercharger pulleys and upgraded intercooler heat exchangers, unlocking immense power without ever stressing the factory connecting rods or pistons.)",
