      "Harmonic Balancer Separation: The rubber isolator in the original harmonic balancer/crank pulley degrades from age and heat. The outer heavy metal ring separates and violently machines its way through the timing cover.",
      "Engine Mount Collapse: The massive weight and immense torque of the 5.4L V8 completely crushes the fluid-filled engine mounts over time, causing severe vibrations in the cabin at idle.",
      "16 Spark Plugs Maintenance: The unique twin-spark V8 design means buying and replacing 16 spark plugs and 16 ignition wires. Neglecting this stresses the 8 ignition coils.",
      "Rear Main Seal Leak: The rear main seal between the engine and transmission frequently develops a slow oil weep over high mileages."
