    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM646 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. Inherited directly from the legendary OM611, this heavy-duty timing system is a genuine 'lifetime' component that will rarely, if ever, require servicing or replacement before the engine reaches 400 000 to 500 000 kilometers, provided basic 10 000 km oil change intervals with high-quality synthetic oil are strictly respected. The chain guides are robust, and the engine entirely avoids the catastrophic timing chain stretching issues of the gasoline engines.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC16C2 (This represents the refined Generation 2 Common Rail system. It utilizes an engine-driven high-pressure pump (often CP3) that pressurizes the fuel rail up to an impressive 1 600 bar. It features highly refined 7-hole injectors that deliver microscopic bursts of fuel directly into the combustion chambers. This multi-injection strategy drastically reduces the violent diesel clatter, improving emissions and creating an incredibly smooth torque curve. While the infamous 'Black Death' injector seal failure is less common than on the predecessor, it remains a critical vulnerability that must be monitored.)",
    engineLifespan: "500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM646 cast-iron engine block is legendary for its durability. Because this specific C 220 CDI Fleet variant is artificially software-restricted to exactly 100 kW to slip under specific tax brackets, the internal rotating assembly, turbocharger, and cooling system experience absolutely zero mechanical stress. The engine will effortlessly outlast the W203 chassis. The facelifted W203 chassis also largely resolved the catastrophic structural rust and electrical gremlins of the earlier models, significantly improving the overall economic lifespan. The true enemies are failing intake swirl flaps and clogged DPF systems.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) turbocharger. The variable vanes dynamically adjust exhaust gas velocity to spool the compressor instantly off idle, entirely eliminating traditional turbo lag and providing the full 340 Nm of peak torque at a very low 2 000 RPM. Because the engine is restricted to 136 horsepower, the turbo operates well below its thermal limits. However, the variable vanes are highly prone to becoming clogged with hard carbon soot if the car is driven exclusively in slow, stop-and-go taxi traffic, triggering Limp Mode.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16C2 (A highly sophisticated, lightning-fast electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates the 1600 bar common rail pressure monitoring, precise VNT turbo actuation, and the new electronically actuated EGR valve. This specific ECU is hard-coded with a severe mapping restriction to limit the engine to exactly 100 kW (136 hp). However, because this engine shares almost all its critical hardware with the 150 horsepower C 220 CDI, the EDC16 ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to completely erase the tax handicap via the diagnostic port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4 (Often equipped with DPF depending on market/year)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "220+ hp (The heavy cast-iron block, lowered 17.5:1 compression ratio, and forged internals of the OM646 are vastly overbuilt. The limiting factor for horsepower is the small stock VNT turbocharger and the flow capacity of the factory injectors. The bottom end can easily handle massive boost. Upgrading to a larger turbocharger from the 2.7L or 3.2L engines and fitting larger injector nozzles unlocks immense power without ever stressing the connecting rods.)",
