    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM646 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. Inherited directly from the legendary OM611, this heavy-duty timing system is a genuine 'lifetime' component that will rarely, if ever, require servicing or replacement before the engine reaches 400 000 to 500 000 kilometers, provided basic 10 000 km oil change intervals with high-quality synthetic oil are strictly respected. The chain guides are highly robust, and the engine entirely avoids the catastrophic timing chain stretching issues of the gasoline engines.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC16C31 (This represents the refined Generation 2 Common Rail system tailored for DPF compliance. It utilizes a CP3 high-pressure pump that pressurizes the fuel rail up to 1 600 bar. It features highly refined 7-hole injectors that deliver microscopic bursts of fuel directly into the combustion chambers. This multi-injection strategy drastically reduces the violent diesel clatter, dramatically improves emissions, and aids in exhaust temperature management for DPF regeneration. While the infamous 'Black Death' injector seal failure is less common than on the predecessor, it remains a critical vulnerability.)",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM646 cast-iron engine block is legendary for its durability. Because this engine is exceptionally over-engineered, the internal rotating assembly, turbocharger, and cooling system handle the 150 horsepower with absolute ease. The engine will effortlessly outlast the W203 chassis. The facelifted W203 chassis also largely resolved the catastrophic structural rust and electrical gremlins of the earlier models, significantly improving the overall economic lifespan of the vehicle. The true enemies are failing intake swirl flaps and a terminally clogged Diesel Particulate Filter.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with an advanced Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) turbocharger. The variable vanes dynamically adjust exhaust gas velocity to spool the compressor instantly off idle, entirely eliminating traditional turbo lag and providing the full 340 Nm of peak torque at a very low 2 000 RPM. The turbo operates well below its thermal limits. However, the variable vanes are highly prone to becoming clogged with hard carbon soot if the car is driven exclusively in slow, stop-and-go city traffic, triggering Limp Mode.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16C31 (A highly sophisticated, lightning-fast electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates the 1600 bar common rail pressure monitoring, precise VNT turbo actuation, the electronically actuated EGR valve, and the complex DPF regeneration cycles. The ECU actively monitors exhaust backpressure and temperatures to trigger diesel post-injection for burning off soot. The EDC16 ECU is incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to easily unlock massive performance gains via the diagnostic port.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4 (Factory DPF Equipped)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "220+ hp (The heavy cast-iron block, lowered 17.5:1 compression ratio, and forged internals of the OM646 are vastly overbuilt. The limiting factor for horsepower is the small stock VNT turbocharger and the strict flow limits of the factory DPF. The bottom end can easily handle massive boost. Upgrading to a larger turbocharger and performing a DPF delete (where legally permitted) unlocks immense power without ever stressing the connecting rods.)",
