      "Intake Manifold Swirl Flap Failure: The plastic swirl flaps inside the intake manifold become coated in thick, sticky EGR soot. The linkage wears out, and the flaps can break off and be ingested by the engine, causing catastrophic damage.",
      "Injector Seal Failure (Black Death): The copper crush washer sealing the fuel injector to the cylinder head degrades. High-pressure combustion gas escapes, baking raw diesel fuel into a solid, black, tar-like rock that buries the injectors.",
      "Thermostat Failure: The thermostat frequently fails open, preventing the engine from ever reaching the optimal 87°C operating temperature, absolutely ruining fuel economy and permanently preventing DPF regeneration.",
      "722.6 Automatic Transmission 13-Pin Connector Leak: The 5-speed electronic transmission frequently leaks ATF from the 13-pin pilot bushing. Capillary action draws the fluid up the wiring harness directly into the TCM."
