    yearRange: "2000-2003",
    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The OM612 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. Unlike modern lightweight diesel engines, this timing system is massively over-engineered. It is a true 'lifetime' component that will rarely, if ever, require servicing or replacement before the engine reaches 400 000 to 500 000 kilometers, provided basic 10 000 km oil change intervals with high-quality synthetic oil are strictly respected. The chain guides are robust, though the hydraulic chain tensioner can occasionally stick at extreme mileages, causing a brief cold-start rattle.)",
    injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection / Bosch EDC15C6 (This early Generation 1 Common Rail system utilizes an engine-driven high-pressure pump (CP1) that pressurizes a single fuel rail up to 1 350 bar. Bosch solenoid injectors deliver precise bursts of fuel directly into the combustion chambers. While incredibly efficient and brutally torquey, this early CDI system is plagued by the infamous 'Black Death'—a critical failure where the copper crush washers sealing the injectors to the cylinder head fail, allowing combustion gases and tar-like diesel sludge to bury the five injectors permanently.)",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 500 000+ km (The mechanical core of the OM612 cast-iron engine block is globally renowned for its legendary durability. Because this specific C 270 CDI variant is heavily over-engineered, the internal rotating assembly, turbocharger, and cooling system handle the 170 horsepower effortlessly. The engine will comfortably outlast the early W203 chassis. The true enemies of this vehicle's lifespan are catastrophic structural rust on the bodywork, the 'Black Death' injector seal failure destroying the cylinder head, and the fragile plastic intake swirl flaps.)",
    turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a highly robust Garrett GT2256V Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) turbocharger. The variable vanes adjust exhaust gas flow to spool the turbo quickly, providing the full, unrestricted 400 Nm of peak torque at a very low 1 800 RPM. The turbo operates well below its thermal limits. However, the variable vanes are highly prone to sticking if the car is driven exclusively in stop-and-go city traffic, causing underboost codes and forcing the car into Limp Mode.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC15C6 (A highly sophisticated and reliable electronic diesel control module. It perfectly integrates common rail pressure monitoring, VNT turbo actuation, and the electronic EGR valve. Unlike the manual version, this ECU mapping permits the full 400 Nm of torque because the 5-speed automatic can easily handle it. The ECU is fully OBD-II compliant and incredibly receptive to software flashing, allowing tuners to unlock massive performance gains.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "250+ hp (The heavy cast-iron block and forged internals of the OM612 5-cylinder are vastly overbuilt. The limiting factor for horsepower is the stock GT2256V turbocharger and the flow capacity of the standard Bosch injectors. The bottom end can easily handle over 2.0 bar of boost. Because this variant is paired with the indestructible 722.6 automatic transmission, it can be tuned aggressively without worrying about destroying a clutch.)",
