      "Turbo Inlet Seal Leak (EKAS Failure): The orange rubber seal connecting the plastic intake to the turbocharger tears easily. Oily PCV vapor drips directly onto the electronic swirl flap (EKAS) motor beneath it, shorting it out and causing Limp Mode.",
      "7G-Tronic (722.9) Conductor Plate: The 7-speed transmission frequently suffers from speed sensor failures on the internal conductor plate, locking the car in Limp Mode.",
      "DPF & Exhaust Sensor Failure: The hyper-sensitive North American emissions software will immediately throw the car into Limp Mode if the DPF clogs, or if any differential pressure/EGT sensors fail.",
      "Piezo Injector Failure: The high-tech injectors can fail internally or stick open, causing rough idling, white smoke, or even melting a piston if ignored.",
      "EGR Valve Seizure: The electronic EGR valve becomes jammed with thick, sticky soot, suffocating the engine's intake tract."
