    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M272 utilizes a robust double-row timing chain. Because the C 300 was introduced later in the M272's lifecycle, these engines safely fall outside the infamous balance shaft defect serial number range that plagued earlier models. Therefore, the timing system in this specific US-market W204 is considered a highly durable, lifetime component, provided the engine receives regular high-quality synthetic oil changes.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system. Because this specific variant is E85 Flex-Fuel compatible, it utilizes specially coated, high-flow fuel injectors, hardened fuel lines, and a specialized fuel pump to handle the highly corrosive nature of ethanol. The ECU uses advanced oxygen and fuel composition sensors to dynamically adjust fueling trims on the fly depending on the ethanol blend in the tank. The system is extremely reliable and completely avoids the carbon buildup issues inherent to later direct-injected CGI engines.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the all-aluminum M272 V6 engine block in the W204 chassis is exceptional. By completely avoiding the balance shaft metallurgy issues of the older generation, it is an incredibly robust, deeply refined V6. The W204 chassis also completely eradicated the structural rust issues of the past. The engine will easily outlast the vehicle with basic maintenance. However, frequently switching between pure E85 and regular gasoline without giving the ECU time to adapt fuel trims can cause temporary rough running.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M272 relies entirely on its 3.0-liter displacement, high 11.3:1 compression ratio, and continuously variable valve timing on all four camshafts to generate its incredibly smooth power delivery. Because it lacks forced induction, it completely avoids complex supercharger or turbocharger maintenance issues, making the engine bay significantly simpler and highly reliable.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly advanced engine management system mapped specifically for the North American market to meet strict EPA emissions and handle E85 Flex-Fuel dynamic mapping. The ECU actively monitors ethanol content to drastically increase fuel injector pulse widths when running on E85, as ethanol has a much lower energy density than gasoline. Tuning potential is practically nonexistent due to the naturally aspirated nature of the engine.)",
    euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 2 / ULEV-II",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 3.0-liter M272 is vastly overbuilt. However, because it is naturally aspirated, extracting any meaningful horsepower is virtually impossible without completely disassembling the engine. While E85 has a higher octane rating, the engine's fixed compression ratio prevents it from fully utilizing the ethanol for massive power gains without forced induction.)",
