    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M272 utilizes a highly robust double-row timing chain. Unlike the catastrophic single-row chains of the 4-cylinder M271 engines, this duplex chain is generally a true lifetime component. Furthermore, because the W204 was introduced in 2007, the vast majority of these 3.5L V6 engines completely avoided the infamous balance shaft chain sprocket metallurgy defect that destroyed early W203 and W211 models. Assuming the engine serial number is verified to be past the defective range, the timing system is exceptionally reliable, only requiring periodic inspection of the chain tensioner at very high mileages.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system. It utilizes modern electronic throttle control and a highly sensitive Hot-Film Mass Air Flow (MAF) sensor. The system is extremely reliable and completely avoids the capillary oil wicking issues that plagued the 4-cylinder engines. Furthermore, because it uses traditional port injection, it completely avoids the severe carbon buildup issues on the intake valves that cripple the later direct-injected CGI engines. However, the variable-length intake manifold uses fragile plastic swirl flap arms that frequently break and trigger performance issues.)",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 450 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the all-aluminum 3.5L M272 V6 engine block in the W204 chassis is exceptional. By avoiding the balance shaft failures of the older generation and the carbon buildup of the newer CGI engines, it is arguably the most robust V6 available in the early W204 lineup. The W204 chassis completely eradicated the structural rust issues of the past. The engine will easily outlast the vehicle with basic maintenance, provided the intake manifold swirl flaps and the thermostat are proactively addressed when they fail.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M272 relies entirely on its massive 3.5-liter displacement, 10.7:1 compression ratio, and continuously variable valve timing on all four camshafts to generate its incredibly smooth power delivery. Because it lacks forced induction, it completely avoids complex supercharger or turbocharger maintenance issues, making the engine bay significantly simpler, cooler, and highly reliable.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 (A highly advanced, lightning-fast engine management system designed to tightly control emissions and precisely manage the continuously variable valve timing. The ECU is incredibly robust and mounts securely on top of the engine block. Because this is a naturally aspirated engine mapped close to its natural volumetric efficiency limits, tuning potential is practically nonexistent, making the ECU a 'leave it alone' component.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4 / Euro 5",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the 3.5-liter M272 is vastly overbuilt. However, because it is naturally aspirated, extracting any meaningful horsepower is virtually impossible without completely disassembling the engine. While the block can theoretically handle forced induction via aftermarket supercharger kits like Kleemann, doing so places immense stress on the high-compression pistons and is generally not financially viable.)",
