    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M156 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. However, the true fatal flaw of the timing and valvetrain system lies in the camshafts and the hydraulic lifters. The engine suffers from camshaft lobe wear due to inadequate lubrication to the top end during cold starts. While the Performance Package Plus (P31) introduced SLS AMG internal components, the camshafts and buckets still require meticulous oil intervals. Additionally, while most P31 package cars were built after the M156 head bolt revision in mid-2010, very early 2010 P31 models may still have the defective head bolts that stretch and snap. Verification via engine serial number is absolutely mandatory.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 AMG (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system mapped specifically by AMG. Unlike modern AMG engines, the M156 uses traditional port injection rather than direct injection. This was a deliberate choice to allow the massive 6.2-liter engine to breathe freely and rev aggressively to its 7,200 RPM redline. Because it uses port injection, the M156 completely avoids the severe carbon buildup issues that plague modern engines, making the intake tract virtually maintenance-free. The fuel delivery is violently responsive.)",
    engineLifespan: "150 000 - 300 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the M156 P31 is vastly superior to the base model IF the engine falls outside the defective head bolt range. The P31 package utilizes forged SLS AMG pistons, lightweight connecting rods, and a revised crankshaft, which collectively shed 3 kilograms of rotating mass from the engine. This makes the engine significantly more rev-happy and durable under extreme loads. If the oil is changed religiously every 5 000 km, the core engine block is remarkably robust. The engine consumes oil by design, so running it low will immediately destroy the camshafts.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The M156 relies entirely on its gargantuan 6.2-liter displacement, high 11.3:1 compression ratio, and aggressive camshaft profiles to generate power. Because it lacks forced induction, it delivers an utterly visceral, instantaneous throttle response that modern turbocharged AMG engines simply cannot replicate. The P31's lighter rotating assembly makes the power delivery even more violently aggressive and linear, screaming toward the redline.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 AMG (A highly advanced, lightning-fast engine management system completely bespoke to AMG. In the Performance Package Plus, the ECU mapping is revised to allow the throttle bodies to open wider than the base C 63, liberating an extra 30 horsepower directly from the factory. While the P31 is closer to the engine's true potential, aftermarket tuning can still optimize the fueling and spark for minor gains.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "650+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the P31 package is genuinely race-grade. Featuring authentic SLS AMG forged pistons, lightweight connecting rods, and a strengthened crankshaft, the bottom end is immensely strong. With long-tube headers and a tune, the engine comfortably pushes 550+ hp naturally aspirated. Bolting on an aftermarket supercharger kit can easily push this forged block past 700+ hp, limited only by the MCT transmission clutches.)",
