    timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M156 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex (double-row) timing chain. Because the DR 520 was produced in 2010, it is incredibly risky regarding the M156 head bolt issue. Some DR 520 models may have the defective head bolts that stretch and snap, mixing coolant with engine oil. Verification via engine serial number is absolutely mandatory. Furthermore, the true fatal flaw of the valvetrain remains: the camshafts and the hydraulic lifters. The camshaft lobes are prone to severe wear if oil intervals are neglected or the car is aggressively driven while cold.)",
    injectionType: "Manifold Injection / Bosch ME 9.7 AMG (A highly sophisticated sequential electronic fuel injection system. Unlike modern AMG engines, the M156 uses traditional port injection rather than direct injection. This was a deliberate choice to allow the massive 6.2-liter engine to breathe freely and rev aggressively to its 7,200 RPM redline without the flow limitations of early direct injection systems. Because it uses port injection, the M156 completely avoids the severe carbon buildup issues that plague modern engines. The fuel delivery is violently responsive, matched perfectly to the aggressive ECU mapping of the DR 520.)",
    engineLifespan: "150 000 - 300 000+ km (The mechanical lifespan of the DR 520 engine is entirely bifurcated by the head bolt issue. If the engine has NOT had its head bolts replaced with the updated design, it is a ticking time bomb that will eventually hydrolock or spin a bearing from coolant-diluted oil. If the head bolts are updated, the lifters replaced with SLS AMG 'black series' buckets, and the oil changed religiously every 5 000 km, the core engine block is remarkably robust. The engine consumes oil by design, so running it low will immediately destroy the soft camshafts.)",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The DR 520 relies entirely on its gargantuan 6.2-liter displacement, high 11.3:1 compression ratio, and aggressive camshaft profiles to generate 520 horsepower natively. Because it lacks forced induction, it delivers an utterly visceral, instantaneous throttle response that modern turbocharged AMG engines simply cannot replicate. The power delivery is violently linear, building into a thunderous crescendo at 7,200 RPM.)",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 AMG (A highly advanced, lightning-fast engine management system completely bespoke to AMG. In the extremely rare, UK-only DR 520 limited edition (only 20 units built), the ECU was heavily remapped, and the engine received SLS AMG internal components to fully unleash the true potential of the 6.2L block, pushing output to a staggering 520 horsepower natively from the dealership.)",
    euroStandard: "Euro 5",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "650+ hp (The internal rotating assembly of the DR 520 is genuinely race-grade. Featuring authentic SLS AMG forged pistons, lightweight connecting rods, and a strengthened crankshaft, the bottom end is immensely strong. With long-tube headers and a tune, the engine comfortably pushes 570+ hp naturally aspirated. Bolting on an aftermarket supercharger kit can easily push this forged block past 700+ hp, limited only by the 7G-Tronic transmission clutches and rear tire traction.)",
